WEBVTT

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:04.340
I began a Duel with Number 96.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.490
But, because of Vector's cowardly trap, 
whenever 96 takes damage,

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:10.980
Yuma's placed in danger!

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.770
<i>How should I handle this Duel...?</i>

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:20.860
Yuma!

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.640
Damn you...Vector! That's really low!

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.750
That's a nice view there, dear Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.250
Lay down, Yuma!

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.650
You understand, don't you, Astral?

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:46.880
That this Duel is entirely under my control!

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.600
In order to damage 96,

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.140
he has to activate the traps and attack Yuma...!

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.560
It's the same as Astral being unable to attack at all.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.140
That's disgusting...!

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.400
I set two cards face-down and end my turn!

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:07.830
My turn! Draw!

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.010
I Summon Malicevorous Knife!

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:16.590
And then I activate Malicevorous Knife's effect!

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.820
When this card is Summoned successfully,

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.980
I can Special Summon one Malicevorous Monster from my Graveyard!

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:28.630
Come back to me, my second Malicevorous Knife!

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:34.100
Now, Astral, let me show you the Number I got from these ruins!

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.870
I Overlay the two Level Two Malicevorous Knives!

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:43.970
I use these two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:46.080
Xyz Summon!

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:50.580
Show yourself, Number 65!

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:55.680
The Cursed Executioner that shall carry out your judgment!

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:59.340
Judge Buster the Adjudicutting Djinn!

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:05.860
What's the deal with this Number?
 I feel some unknown presence...

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:09.540
I attack Aspiring Emperor - Hope with Black Mist!

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:13.250
At this moment, I activate Black Mist's effect!

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.710
By detaching one Overlay Unit, I halve the opposing Monster's Attack Power,

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.080
and add that same amount to Black Mist's Attack Power!

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:24.180
What's wrong, Astral?!

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.660
Aren't you going to activate the effect of the Exchange Robe Guard equipped to Hope?!

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.010
Astral, use the effect!

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:36.250
If you do, he'll take damage equal the change in Hope's Attack Power!

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.490
That's <i>right</i>! You <i>can't</i> use it!

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:44.660
In that case, Black Mist will tear Hope to <i>shreds</i>!

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.790
I activate Hope's effect!

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:53.690
By detaching one Overlay Unit, it negates the attack of one Monster on the field!

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.250
Moon Barrier!

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:01.150
In that case, I activate Judge Buster's effect!

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.530
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.520
when a Monster on the field activates its effect,

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:10.510
it negates that Monster Effect's activation!

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:18.690
And then, this effect damages the opposing player by 500 points!

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:24.320
Black Mist's effect hasn't ended yet!

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:27.760
This time for real, it'll beat Hope to a pulp!

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.560
I'm far from done!

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:39.060
Judge Buster attacks Astral directly!

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:12.660
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:15.710
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:23.170
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:26.720
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.600
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:37.940
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:41.150
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:44.030
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:48.660
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:51.740
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:04:51.740 --> 00:05:00.210
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:16.750
Astral!

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.290
Astral!

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:24.420
"Realm of Chaos: Number 96,
 the Incarnation of Insanity!!"

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:22.130
S-Shit...!

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.590
Astral...!

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.630
Yuma!

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:30.260
Watching you squirm and cry just makes my day!

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.890
I'll end my turn there.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:36.230
Orbital, are you absolutely certain?

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.980
Yes! There was a change in spatial pressure around Area 34!

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:42.280
Is it a Barian?

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.900
My turn! Draw!

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.700
I activate the Magic Card, Xyz Treasure!

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:53.540
For each Xyz Monster I have on the field,

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.960
I can draw one card from my deck.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.790
I have two Monsters on the field.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.380
Thus, I draw two cards.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.340
Then I Summon Bakudan!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:09.260
This card can be equipped to one Xyz Monster the opponent controls on the field.

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.760
Go, Bakudan!

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:13.720
Equip onto Black Mist!

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:21.190
When the equipped Xyz has zero Overlay Units while equipped with Bakudan,

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:23.070
it blows up and is destroyed.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:26.900
Black Mist has only one Overlay Unit.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:30.200
In other words, if you activates its effect one more time,

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.530
it will automatically explode and destroy itself.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.250
Tch! What a shrewd trick!

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:42.080
I see. Now he can damage Number 96 and destroy Black Mist.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.920
Awesome, Astral!

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.300
How foolish.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.760
I activate Judge Master's effect!

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:52.800
When one Monster on the field uses its effect,

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:59.140
I can detach one Overlay Unit to negate the activation of that Monster's effect!

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.940
Now Bakudan's effect is gone!

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:09.070
Then, Astral, you take 500 points of damage!

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:14.700
Astral!

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.920
Bakudan's only got 100 Attack Points!

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:27.510
With Small Stopper, all Monsters with 1000 or less Attack Points can't attack!

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:31.510
And if Attack Position Monsters don't attack,

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:35.470
the player will take 1000 points of damage at the end of their turn.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.180
It's over for you, Astral!

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:40.890
You can't tell how a match will end until the very end!

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:42.900
That's what a Duel is!

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.060
Why won't you be honest with yourself?

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.400
With your loss, I mean!

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:48.900
You think that's the case?

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:49.820
What?

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:55.200
I activate the Magic Card, Release Ticket!

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.910
This card activates by releasing one Monster on the field,

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:03.960
and this card can be treated as two releases.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:10.340
Using this effect, I Summon Swordsman of the Sealing Swords from my hand in Defense Position!

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:17.560
Swordsman of the Sealing Swords can negate one Monster's attack,

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:21.390
and it can't be destroyed in battle once per turn.

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:27.060
I get it! If it's in Defense Position, the effect of Small Stopper won't harm him!

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:27.730
Yuma!

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:33.030
So he can negate the opponent's attack and protect it from destruction in battle.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.450
And it's got high Defense Power.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:37.530
It's definitely impregnable defense.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:39.580
You can do this, Astral!

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:41.750
Hmph. Not bad.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:46.500
I told you. You don't know how a match will end until the very end.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:49.840
But your Life is already down to 100.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.090
What do you plan to do?

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:57.720
Humans get caught by their insignificant friendship nonsense and their camaraderie!

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:01.520
Yet they're fine betraying their friends for their own benefit.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.730
They just throw away their relationships and the bonds they share with their friends!

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:12.820
Astral, you've been tainted by
 Yuma Tsukumo and human weakness!

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:17.200
You won't be able to carry out your original mission that way.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:18.820
What do you mean by that?

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.750
Why do you think you can't absorb Chaos Numbers?

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:26.000
That's because...

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.670
you don't have my power!

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:36.220
If you don't have me, you won't be able to gather all of the Numbers.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:41.600
You aren't qualified to obtain the Numeron Code!

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:46.730
Then he just needs to defeat you right here!

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:48.940
Forget about me! Just do it!

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.480
The time hasn't come yet.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.280
I will end my turn with this.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:59.200
My turn! Draw!

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:01.330
I'm working together with the Barians!

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:05.040
Let me show you just what that means!

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:09.790
I activate the Rank-Up Magic, Barian's Force!

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:11.960
Barian's Force...?

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:16.720
This card ranks up an Xyz Monster on my field,

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:19.220
and evolves it into a Chaos Xyz.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:23.350
I Overlay the Level Two Judge Buster!

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:28.190
I rebuild the Overlay Network using this one Monster!

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.520
Chaos Xyz Change!

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:37.400
Come out! Chaos Number 65!

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:42.030
Great Demon King filled with endless malice and judgment!

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:49.710
The Judging Devil King - Judge Devil!

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:53.130
So that's his...

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:54.590
Chaos Number?

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.260
I activate Judge Devil's effect!

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.760
When I have this Monster on the field,

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:04.260
I can negate the effects of 
my opponent's Monsters and their activation!

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:10.520
Now you can't activate your effect that negates destruction!

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.310
Your impregnable defense was just wasted!

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.070
Too bad for you!

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:19.110
But Swordsman of the Sealing Swords still has 2400 Defense Points!

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.320
You can't destroy it by battle!

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:23.070
You sure about that?

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:27.450
I activate Judge Devil's other effect!

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:30.460
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:37.090
it can lower one of the opponent's Monsters' Attack or Defense Power by 1000!

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:44.930
Now, Black Mist, crush the Swordsman of Sealing Swords!

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.560
I've still got more where that came from!

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:54.860
I use Judge Devil to Direct Attack Astral!

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:57.440
Not good...! If he gets hit by that...

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:59.570
Astral will lose!

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.660
Trap, activate! Xyz Reborn!

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.370
It revives an Xyz Monster from my Graveyard!

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:11.210
Be reborn! Number 39, Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.710
Also, Xyz Reborn will

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:18.090
become an Overlay Unit for the revived Xyz Monster!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.970
Tch... What useless struggling.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:24.890
Judge Devil, cancel your attack.

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:30.100
But you can't use your Monster Effects as long as Judge Devil remains here!

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:33.310
And above that, you can't even attack me!

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.650
Whatever path you choose, you're done for!

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:36.860
Astral...

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:42.820
It's my fault... In order to protect me, Astral...

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:47.660
If only you could Duel like you normally do...

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:52.710
If he loses the Duel and Astral disappears...

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:54.790
I... I...!

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.420
Raise your head!

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.550
Never take your eyes off the enemy standing before you!

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:02.340
You must face one another with all you have.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.590
Think about what you're capable of doing right now.

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:08.720
Wh-What the heck can I do?!

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.890
Tell me, Astral!

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:12.430
Stop your whiny sniveling!

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:18.270
Astral...

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.780
<i>What I can do...</i>

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:24.860
<i>What I should be doing right now...</i>

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:33.790
<i>Figure it out, Yuma. If it's you, you should be able to...</i>

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:37.290
That's it! That's right!

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:41.000
<i>I have to escape from here by any means necessary!</i>

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.500
<i>That's all there is to it!</i>

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:46.720
<i>That's...</i>

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:50.180
<i>If only I could jump to the other pillar.</i>

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:52.350
<i>But how do I do that?</i>

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.400
Th-That's it!

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:03.940
Have you finished saying your goodbyes to Yuma?!

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:05.990
This Duel isn't over yet.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:10.570
Your Life's a mere 100. What can you possibly do?

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.120
You bastard...!

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:19.880
I set one card and end my turn!

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:25.260
<i>But if I fail... I...</i>

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:30.050
This is... one of my dad's coins.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:35.430
That's right! Astral's already fighting his Duel to the limit!

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:41.270
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:42.650
What?!

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:43.900
- Yuma!
 - Yuma!

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:00.620
Don't think you can get away!

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:11.760
Go, Astral!

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:14.720
Beat the crap outta that guy 'til you feel satisfied!

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:16.100
Yuma...

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:19.440
Damn you, Yuma!

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.520
But my overwhelming victory has not changed!

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:25.270
Don't be so sure.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:26.230
What?!

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.700
I've already completed my formula for victory.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:32.990
My turn! Draw!

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:40.000
I use Aspiring Emperor - Hope as Xyz Material to Chaos Xyz!

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:46.500
Come out, Chaos Number 39!

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:49.260
The messenger changing all to chaos!

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:52.010
Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray!

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:59.060
Trap, activate Superior Overlay!

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:04.900
If the number of Xyz Materials of one Xyz Monster I control

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:09.740
outnumbers the combined Overlay Units of all Xyz Monsters my opponent controls, this card activates

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:12.530
and it destroys all of my opponent's Monsters!

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:16.580
Astral has two Overlay Units attached to Hope.

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:20.120
And 96 only has one on Black Mist.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:24.460
I-Impossible...! You're going to destroy my Monsters?!

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:28.920
However, if you use your Overlay Unit to stop this effect,

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:31.590
you can stop your Monsters' destruction.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:34.720
What will you do, Number 96?

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:42.100
I detach one Overlay Unit to stop Black Mist's destruction!

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:48.520
Heck yeah! Now that he used his Overlay Units,

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:50.480
he can't use that effect anymore!

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:54.070
I can't believe it...! He turned things around in just two turns with a single card?!

00:16:55.280 --> 00:17:01.080
Impossible! Are you saying you
 anticipated this situation would occur?!

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.000
That's right.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.000
You bastard!

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:11.050
I figured you'd try to make me waver by taking Yuma hostage and trying to keep me from attacking.

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:14.380
You dare make a fool out of me?!

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:18.350
I activate Hope Ray's effect!

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:24.730
By detaching one Overlay Unit, I can raise Hope Ray's Attack Power by 500 points!

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.480
Overlay Charge!

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:36.070
Then, by detaching an Overlay Unit, I can decrease the opponent's Monster's Attack Power by 1000!

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:39.240
Your loss has just been decided!

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:41.990
I... I...!

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:44.330
Go, Hope Ray!

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:47.920
Hope Ray! Attack Black Mist!

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.300
I will not allow this to go as you want!

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:53.380
Trap, activate!

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.470
Chaos Return!

00:17:56.130 --> 00:18:00.430
When the opponent attacks, this card negates that attack!

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:03.720
What?!

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:08.770
Then, by discarding a card from my hand, I can activate a Magic Card from my Graveyard!

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:13.940
I activate the Rank-Up Magic, Barian's Force, from my Graveyard!

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:28.420
I Overlay the Rank Two Black Mist!

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:33.880
I rebuild the Overlay Network with this one Monster!

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:36.170
Chaos Xyz Change!

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:44.260
Show yourself, Chaos Number 96!

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:49.100
Create a storm of chaos!

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.440
Then descend before us!

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:58.110
Black Storm!

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.370
He turned Black Mist into a Chaos?!

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:20.220
Now you will no longer be able to absorb me!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:23.390
He turned himself into a Chaos!

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:27.810
I activate Chaos Return's other effect!

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:31.190
The Monster whose attack was negated by this card's effect

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:34.400
must attack once again!

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:35.400
What?!

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:37.940
He stopped the attack only to force him to attack?

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.200
Why did he stop the attack the first time?

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:43.530
I activate Black Storm's effect!

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:47.660
When this guy is destroyed by battle, all Battle Damage I take

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:49.500
is inflicted on the opposing player!

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:16.610
A-A tie...

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.110
Number 96...!

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:24.200
Astral...!

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:29.160
Now that it's come to this, I'll kill everyone in this temple at once!

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:34.420
What the?!

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:46.390
Astral... we'll settle this later.

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:49.140
Number 96...

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:51.810
Yuma!

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:56.270
Kaito!

00:20:57.560 --> 00:20:58.900
Why are you here?!

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:00.570
I'll explain later!

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.290
The Seven Numbers hidden in the ruins...?

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:14.330
Yeah.

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:19.840
But this time it was stolen by the Barians.

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:21.510
<i>Astral...</i>

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:29.470
That was a close one. But at least the Number is safe.

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:31.930
I don't like it.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:37.310
You use some boring tricks.
 You're a real second-rate villain.

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:38.900
What'd you say?!

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:39.440
See ya!

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:43.820
I'll come see you if I have another job for you, my servant!

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:46.360
Hey! Wait!

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:47.820
Just let him be.

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:49.120
Don Thousand!

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:52.240
Everything is going as planned.

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:56.040
Anyway, you have something else you need to do.

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:56.960
What?!

00:21:57.710 --> 00:22:02.050
It's about time for those two to wake up...

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:24.030
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:26.570
<i>Or maybe you're the one who's not gettin' serious?</i>

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:27.780
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:29.200
<i>Do I understand?</i>

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:32.080
<i>Already got my answers</i>

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:34.580
<i>Once you start movin', you ain't stoppin'</i>

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:37.120
<i>I go on thinkin' even while losin'.</i>

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:38.210
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:39.250
<i>I understand!</i>

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:42.630
<i>Our formula for reversal's already gathered</i>

00:22:42.630 --> 00:22:44.960
<i>You afraid it ain't comin' true?</i>

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:48.090
<i>I gotta 'least give it a try</i>

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:50.300
<i>Ain't no problem if they say I'm borin'</i>

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:53.310
<i>True failure's when we stop movin'</i>

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:55.270
<i>Come on! Ga, ga, ga, guys & dolls</i>

00:22:55.270 --> 00:22:56.640
<i>Go, go, go, go my way</i>

00:22:56.640 --> 00:22:58.520
<i>Oh, oh, oh, over ray</i>

00:22:58.810 --> 00:23:02.810
<i>Door's always open for you</i>

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:07.900
<i>Bring your power forth and go way, go way</i>

00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:09.150
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:09.150 --> 00:23:13.160
<i>And tears are no way, no way</i>

00:23:13.660 --> 00:23:18.540
<i>With all my strength, pave way, go way</i>

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:19.750
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:23.880
<i>Got all the courage here</i>

00:23:23.880 --> 00:23:26.050
<i>You ought to understand!</i>

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:28.260
<i>Go way, go way</i>

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:43.560
The legendary city with high class, Spartan City.

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:47.280
The airship shows us that this is where the next Number is located in ruins there.

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:51.490
Once we get there, we come across some nostalgic faces.

00:23:52.030 --> 00:23:53.740
There's lots of cute clothes!

00:23:53.950 --> 00:23:55.620
Gauche became a Pro Duelist?!

00:23:55.740 --> 00:23:57.160
Could it be a Barian?!

00:23:57.580 --> 00:23:59.500
What?! A Tag Duel?!

00:24:00.210 --> 00:24:01.870
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:02.210 --> 00:24:05.710
"Alit the Silent Fighter:
 Reunion of the Passionate Duelists!"

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:09.210
Alit! Where'd the old you go?!
